WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:05.665
PongLens is a performance hub for competitive table tennis players.

2
00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:13.351
It has two sides. Players use it to study their own matches. Coaches use it to review their students' matches, and get paid for the work.

3
00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:18.197
Everything on the player side starts with a match you filmed yourself.

4
00:00:19.247 --> 00:00:24.623
Upload the file from your phone, or paste a YouTube link. You get an email when it is ready.

5
00:00:27.073 --> 00:00:32.689
What comes back is the same match with the time between points removed, and every point cut into its own clip.

6
00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:44.155
Playback is built for studying. Hold one side of the screen for double speed, or the other for quarter speed, and zoom in when you want to watch a single shot.

7
00:00:47.805 --> 00:00:51.765
You can replay the point you are on, or jump straight to any other point in the match.

8
00:00:53.215 --> 00:00:57.943
And you can stop on a frame to write a note on that point or draw on it, without leaving the video.

9
00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:08.745
Scoring takes about ten minutes. Each point plays, you say who won it, and the score, the game count and the serve rotation keep themselves up to date.

10
00:01:11.795 --> 00:01:19.259
Once the match is scored you can read it. How you did on serve and receive, how you held up in the close points, and where the match turned.

11
00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:24.461
Score more matches, and the same picture builds over time.

12
00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:32.519
Placement maps show where the ball landed. The corner your opponent kept finding, and the one that kept working for you.

13
00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:42.065
You can share a match with your coach. They watch the real points and leave notes on them, in writing, drawn on the frame, or as a voice note.

14
00:01:44.915 --> 00:01:49.811
Lessons, match notes, and photographs of your notebook pages go into one journal you can search.

15
00:01:51.261 --> 00:01:55.773
You can also ask your journal a question, and it answers from what you have written.

16
00:01:58.623 --> 00:02:04.815
You can also export a point or a whole match with the score on the picture, to post on social media or send to someone as a link.

17
00:02:06.665 --> 00:02:09.785
The other side of PongLens is built for coaches.

18
00:02:10.935 --> 00:02:15.375
A coach decides what a review includes, what it costs, and how many days they need.

19
00:02:18.025 --> 00:02:23.233
What they sell sits on their own page, along with their background and what past students have said about them.

20
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:30.427
Payments run through Stripe. A coach connects it once, and it pays their bank.

21
00:02:33.477 --> 00:02:39.957
When a student buys a review, they send one of their matches and answer the coach's questions. The coach reads the answers before accepting.

22
00:02:42.807 --> 00:02:47.847
The match reaches the coach already cut into points, so there is no scrolling through a video looking for a rally.

23
00:02:49.297 --> 00:02:55.417
The coach watches it point by point. Everything they notice becomes a pattern, with every point where it happened attached to it.

24
00:02:57.867 --> 00:03:03.723
They can speak the write-up instead of typing it, and PongLens checks it is complete before it is sent.

25
00:03:06.973 --> 00:03:12.517
The student gets the write-up and a clip for every point the coach picked, and Stripe sends the coach their share.

26
00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:20.679
PongLens is free to start. Sign up with Google or an email address, and upload your first match.

27
00:03:22.329 --> 00:03:26.361
PongLens. Film the match once, and study it all year.
